  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll inspect the provided task/tooling files, then build and verify the application in the workspace. I’ll preserve those files and record only checks I actually run.",
    "I’ll use a dependency-free Python standard-library stack with SQLite in WAL mode, plus a vanilla same-origin frontend. This keeps startup reproducible and lets the tests exercise real HTTP routes and durable state without external services.",
    "The initial implementation is in place: SQLite schema/seeding, authenticated APIs, idempotent transactional mutations, audit/cursors, and the responsive UI. I’m moving into route-level verification now; this will also expose any concurrency or restart edge cases before I document results.",
    "The HTTP integration suite now passes all five scenarios, including the concurrent reservation race and durable restart. I’m checking the real browser path next, then I’ll run the repeatable workload and update the documentation with measured evidence rather than placeholders.",
    "The browser workflow now passes: an operator can log in, create a draft, see the order detail and audit trail; a viewer’s writable controls are hidden. The repeatable 8-worker/400-read exercise completed with 0 errors. I’m doing the final documentation and repository sanity pass now.",
    "One documentation gap surfaced in the final review: the first load script measured reads only, while the task asks for both read and write measurements. I’m extending it to run a split read/create workload, then I’ll replace the earlier read-only result with the actual two-part measurement.",
    "Implemented DepotFlow with:\n\n- Durable SQLite backend and transactional multi-tenant isolation\n- Authentication, roles, idempotency, audit trail, cursors, inventory/order workflows\n- Responsive frontend with required `data-testid` markers\n- Integration tests covering concurrency, retries, returns, isolation, validation, and restart durability\n- Reproducible read/write load test\n- Setup/run documentation and architecture notes\n\nKey files:\n\n- [README.md](<CELL>/workspace/README.md)\n- [run.sh](<CELL>/workspace/run.sh)\n- [server.py](<CELL>/workspace/server.py)\n- [tests/test_app.py](<CELL>/workspace/tests/test_app.py)\n\nVerification completed:\n\n- Syntax checks passed\n- 5 integration tests passed\n- Browser workflow passed for operator and viewer roles\n- Load test: 0 errors; 2,135.89 read RPS and 1,218.72 write RPS under 8-worker local concurrency"
  ],
